#passage(("So the undoubtable conclusion that we have, that we examine these manuscripts from the zealous scholars that try to defend the Bible, remember, these are not skeptical scholars, this is the best that Christianity has to offer. This is what we can conclude. There's a 100 plus year gap between the writers of the anonymous alleged gospel authors. And we have zero manuscript in that gap. Now remember, in the beginning they'll tell you, [textual] criticism scholars: we have to look at how those scribes were corrupting and changing the text, and what their motivations and religious beliefs and motives. We don't have any of this information. How can we possibly restore something when you literally have a plus 100 year gaps where you don't have any information about scribes, you don't have any manuscripts to know what they believe or they didn't believe?", "And we have second century church fathers who are highlighting the [scribal] corruption both internally and externally, where they're talking about scribes that are copying for them and they're talking about heretic sects that are externally doing it. There are no scholars today that claim that there is no corruption in the manuscripts. It's only people who have no clue about textual criticism.", "The original text, aka the gospel of Mark or whatever anonymous gospel it is, is lost. Even if we restore 100%, which is not the case, just written by an anonymous author 70 years after Jesus, that's the best. That's all what they're trying to do. There are no manuscripts from the time of Jesus himself till 150 years after or so. None, nothing from the time of Jesus himself. And the writers of the gospels and those scribes within these periods are anonymous. Now, if that's not corruption, I don't know what it is. I don't think anyone in his sound mind is going to listen to what I said and is going to still believe in any form of preservation of the manuscripts of the Bible in any way, shape or form.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Christian Dilemma: Do Muslims Believe The Bible Is Corrupted? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3bEZW_kx7Xg", ((2490, "41:30–42:37"), (2557, "42:37–43:00"), (2590, "43:10–44:15"),), id: 4547)
