#passage(("It's a very simple method of textual criticism. And how you know? It's because you have thousands of manuscripts, if not tens of thousands of manuscripts, if not hundreds of thousands of manuscripts, that are from different locations in the world, not near the Catholic Church, different places in the world, everywhere: Orthodox, Catholic, Ethiopian, all of them. All of them are earlier than 1611. All of them have the verse, but talking about the water, and the blood, and the spirit. So it's impossible that all of those people colluded, because they couldn't have communicated with each other to write the same thing. And the only logical explanation would be that this was the information that was passed down to them in all of these different places. Therefore, it is what we can say is closer to the truth, if it's not the truth of what was written down in that verse.", "On the other hand, if you just have one source that disagrees with tens of thousands of other sources separated by locations, ideologies and dates and times, it is impossible to take that one source over the tens of thousands of people who haven't met each other, which all had different beliefs, in different times, in different places. It's a very simple concept of textual criticism. That's how you know for a fact that this is a corruption.", "Not only that, Mark is another example. The long ending of Mark (16:9-20), for example, the story of the adulterous woman (John 8:1-11), all of these things. Either the versions will remove them, or they will put a note after having them that they don't exist in the earliest manuscripts, a footnote or whatever. Either way it's the same method: it's investigating all of these tens of thousands of manuscripts, which you can access yourself, and looking at them, and they didn't have this, and you see that later on you start having it. So you see manuscripts, not only before, but even manuscripts after, they didn't have it. But we have this irregularity only here. So we know for a fact that a scribe in this location and this time has added this information into the Scripture. Which is what the Quran was saying exactly: people corrupting the Bible, the Scripture of God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “King James Christian Challenges Muslim On Bible Preservation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eSGX_1-ukxw", ((2709, "45:09–45:56"), (2762, "46:02–46:23"), (2799, "46:39–47:26"),), id: 4548)

