#passage(("Daniel Wallace says, \"Every single manuscript we have of any material length has corruptions in it. There is no perfect manuscript. Consequently, we have to look at these manuscripts as corrupt documents, but relatively corrupt. Some are better than others, and we have to look at internal evidence as subjective, but relatively subjective.\"", "He gives us five different types of corruption in the scripture: addition to the text, omission from the text, alteration to the text, complete rewriting of the text, insertions to the text. A variation in manuscripts is a corruption. Daniel Wallace says 400,000 to 500,000 variation between the manuscripts that we have. Remember, I'm bringing you your defender. I can go to Bart Ehrman, who's going to tell you it's more. I can go to Bart Ehrman, who doesn't believe at all you can restore anything, which is the right position anyways. But I'm bringing the people that believe your faith, that are actual Christians, that are the people of your book.", "I change the word God with the word servant: the whole book is gone. Changing one word completely alters the meaning.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Becomes Speechless After Being Presented With The Christian Dilemma! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z_W9m77uuyE", ((1715, "28:35–29:12"), (1768, "29:28–30:40"), (1918, "31:58–32:05"),), id: 4550)
