#passage(("When we bring the information, the Christians want to throw the poor Christian scholar under the bus. Daniel B. Wallace is the premier New Testament scholar, widely considered the leading evangelical expert on Koine Greek grammar and textual criticism. He's highly influential. He is heading many of the biblical translations that were done. He's supervising many of the biblical translations like the NIV and these translations. He's a textual expert. He is the founder of the Center for Study of the New Testament Manuscript, the CSNTM. He digitizes Greek manuscripts and preserves them. He has discovered and identified numerous new manuscripts.", "Academic influence: his intermediate grammar textbook is a standard in many evangelical [seminaries]. Translation work: he's a senior NT editor for the NET Bible, for example, as a consultant for the ESV, TLI, and the NIV. Debater and scholar: he engages in academic debates regarding the reliability of the New Testament text, often balancing the rigorous textual science with conservative theology. He's a conservative Christian. Legacy: he has taught in Dallas Theological Seminary for nearly 40 years, influencing generations of pastors and scholars.", "And it's not only Daniel B. Wallace who says this. Bruce Metzger, his mentor, says the same thing. Philip Comfort says the same thing. They're all the conservative Christian scholars that defend the Bible. Nobody in textual criticism today who defends the Bible will tell you that Daniel B. Wallace isn't the best one in that field today. You could disagree, but nobody will throw him under the bus, cuz he tries to defend Christianity. He's not someone who's trying to attack the religion. But he admits realities. Why is he admitting to them? Because the text is in front of him. It's manuscripts. He can pretend that's not the case, but you can check the manuscripts yourself. You don't have to accept anything that Daniel B. Wallace or anybody says. We can see them now in the manuscripts in front of our own eyes.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Becomes Speechless After Being Presented With The Christian Dilemma! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z_W9m77uuyE", ((2165, "36:05–37:00"), (2222, "37:02–37:36"), (2260, "37:40–38:54"),), id: 4551)
