#passage(("James White is not textual criticism scholar. Nobody goes to James White for text criticism. I'm talking about proper textual criticism scholars. He didn't study specifically textual criticism. Wes is a student. When I say person did not study something, I'm not rejecting. I'm stating facts. You will see that [Wes Huff] is studying in university now. If you go Google right now who are the most popular textual criticism scholars of the New Testament, you're not going to get the names that you're saying.", "Daniel [Wallace] has an entire [lecture] talking about the Bible. What he does is he goes to the stage and he says, look, we have so many thousands of manuscripts of the [Bible]. And then gullible Christians fall for this nonsense. But then he goes on to say it doesn't matter how many manuscripts you have. What matters is the quality of the manuscript. So why did you then sell all of this load of nonsense to the people? Because the people like to hear this nonsense. They think, \"Oh, many manuscripts means good.\" No, actually, your case it means terrible.", "He says there is more variations and corruptions in the manuscripts than the number of words in the Bible. That's what [Ehrman] says, but now I'm bringing your own people saying it.", "The problem is when someone says it doesn't matter that you have thousands or hundreds of thousands, whatever the number is of [variants], because we can know: no, you cannot know. If you don't have an original, you cannot compare and go back to something. You have nothing to go back to. You have nothing from the first 150 years; earliest you have is 400 years later. You cannot know. So if everything you have, the earliest of it, is all contradicting each other, then you cannot know what is what and what was said and what was not said. That's the whole point we're making.", "That's why Danny [Wallace] says if we had the original, the textual criticism doesn't exist. Textual criticism only exists to try to figure out what the original is. It only exists when there is no original. But gullible Christians don't understand this basic common sense. If we have an agreed upon original, then nobody will be doing an entire science to just try and understand what is what. We only do that because we don't know.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Educated Christian Challenges Muslim On Bible Corruption And Textual Criticism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gYYmqGjrSmo", ((2298, "38:18–39:16"), (2382, "39:42–40:37"), (2453, "40:53–41:07"), (2592, "43:12–43:40"), (2620, "43:40–44:05"),), id: 4552)
