#passage(("One of the tactics that you should keep in mind when engaging with critics of Islam is: just let them speak. The more they speak, the more they expose themselves, the more they expose their ignorance, the more ridiculous it gets.", "The Islamic dilemma is all about the Quran in multiple places speaking positively about the [Torah], and affirming that these are scriptures from previous prophets, and that the prophets were sent by Allah, and Islam is naturally a continuation to those previous messages. So the Christian apologists, they look at these verses and they assume, due to this, that the [Torah] and [Injil] are preserved and they're authoritative, even though the Quran says no such thing. Now Muslims of course reject this claim, and they point out that the Quran itself continuously corrects these previous scriptures. So how is it possible for them to be preserved and authentic and authoritative if they're constantly being corrected? So folks like David Wood are asserting that the Quran isn't correcting the [Torah]; the Quran is contradicting them [unintentionally], because the author of The quran's got absolutely no idea what's in the Old and New Testament.",), "Farid Responds, “Sam Shamoun Ruins David Wood's Favorite Argument”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YwdF5O1GM3I", ((0, "0:00–0:14"), (51, "0:51–2:06"),), id: 4651)
