#passage(("Do Muslims believe that the Bible is corrupted? The reason we're going to explore this absurd question, even though it's meaningless at this point anyways, because we already have demonstrated the evidence. So the evidence speaks for itself; it doesn't matter what anybody believes at this point. The evidence has already demonstrated the reality. But the reason we're going to talk about this absurd idea is because you have some Christian evangelists that try and say that the Muslims believe the Bible is not corrupted. Why do they argue this? The reason they argue this is because there's conclusive evidence for the corruption of their Bible. So what they do is, when they talk to the Muslim, they try to appeal to Islam. They're like, \"Islam is going to save my Bible. We cannot talk about actual evidence. So I'm going to say, you know what? To prove that my book is not corrupted, I'm going to use your religion.\" So imagine that you have to argue that your book is preserved by misrepresenting the beliefs of another religion. It's common sense that whatever Islam says, it doesn't change the evidence that we just discussed, and that it is indeed corrupted. But they do that when they talk to Muslims, because they have nothing; they have to hang to a straw man.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Christian Dilemma: Do Muslims Believe The Bible Is Corrupted? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3bEZW_kx7Xg", ((2877, "47:57–49:11"),), id: 4654)
