#passage(("Someone that blurts out 20 plus verses in that short amount of time, in just a few seconds, knows exactly what he's doing. He doesn't want to read the verses for you; he just wants the audience to eat up what he's saying, because he knows that the audience is too lazy to go through all the verses that he mentioned.", "Christians need to be aware, though, that this has got nothing to do with the preservation of the Quran or the preservation of the Bible. If that's the case, then the Muslim that's hearing this and accepting this needs to leave Islam. But that doesn't prove that the Bible is preserved, because once you leave Islam, you no longer trust in Muhammad, peace be upon him. So you would still need some sort of secular approach, or at least some sort of historical approach, to prove that the Bible is preserved and authoritative, which is why [Ijaz] went proper historical, quoting modern Scholars, and treating this in the way it should be treated.",), "Farid Responds, “Response to Sam Shamoun Fresh & Fit Debate on Quranic Preservation”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j8wo1OmaDZU", ((77, "1:17–1:38"), (119, "1:59–3:09"),), id: 4655)

