#passage(("One last evidence I'm going to include is the statements that we have from the Quran, hadith, that mentions information in the Tawra and the Gospel that we cannot find in our hands today. If this information we don't have it in our hands today, and they're supposed to be in the original Tawra and the Gospel, then the Quran is telling us that this we have today is not the Torah and the Gospel, and it's a corrupted scripture. We may have remnants of truth here and there that survived to the seventh century, but we don't have this information that I'm about to show. So this is a clear evidence that the Tawra and the gospel the Quran talks about have been corrupted, or parts of them are lost. They're not found today in their original form.", "Christians today hold certain beliefs, and the Quran explicitly contradicts those beliefs, and it explicitly talks to the Christians. The author of the Quran knows that the Christians believe these things and that they have it in their books. The Quran is explicitly refuting those beliefs, which shows that the Quran is telling us that those beliefs are not the true correct beliefs of the original Torah and gospel that came down upon Moses and that came down upon Jesus, and that is in itself an evidence of corruption.", "So let me give a few examples of information according to the Quran that don't exist in our hands today. For example, in the Quran in chapter 48 29, Allah talks about prophet Muhammad being the messenger of God. And then Allah talks about his companions, and then Allah says: their sign is in their faces from [effect of] prostration. The description is in the Torah. Then Allah says the description of the gospel is as a plant that produces [its] offshoot and strength etc. Allah gives us this description of the companions of the prophet Muhammad. We don't have that description in this way today anywhere.", "Also Allah tells us in the Quran, in chapter 9 verse 111, that Allah indeed has purchased from the believers their lives and their wealth in exchange for paradise. They fight in the cause of Allah, and they kill or they're killed. This is a true promise binding on him, God, in the Torah and the Gospel and the Quran. It's another example. Also Allah says in the Quran 5:32 that we ordained on the children of Israel that whoever takes a life, unless for punishment or mischief in the land, it's as if he killed all of humanity, and whoever saves life, [it's as] if he saved humanity. Many people hear this verse, they know it's in the Quran. And of course, we follow the tradition of those who came before us. This tradition, the true tradition that came from God, is supposed to be in the Tawra; we still follow it so long as it doesn't contradict our tradition. Now, this is supposed to be ordained to the children of Israel. So it has to be in the revelation of God, but we don't find it today. And all of these are clear examples.", "Also, in the hadith, there is a very long hadith. I'm not going to mention the entire hadith, because it's a very, very long hadith, but I'm going to mention a part of it. It is the hadith of [Salman al-Farisi], and it's about his journey accepting Islam. The hadith is authentic, in [Musnad] Ahmed. I'll just give a brief overview. First Salman [Farisi] talks about his conversion story to Christianity, in a way. He wasn't a Christian believer. Then he heard people praying in the church. Then he was impressed. Then he went to his father. He told him: stay on religion [of] your forefathers. Then he asked him: what is the source of this religion? They told him it's in Levant. So then he was waiting for travelers, and then he tried to find people in Levant. Then he found this bishop, and then he saw that this bishop in the church is a liar: he tells people something, and he asked them for money, and he keeps the money to himself. When that bishop died, another person took his place. He praised him for his good character, good manners and all of that. So he went to him to learn from him, and he asked him about his beliefs.", "So that bishop said to [Salman], and this is very important, that I do not know anyone today who is on the same beliefs that I'm upon today. He told him: people have perished, changed and abandoned most of what they were upon. So he's talking about people changing true religion, what the Christianity should have been at that time following Jesus. They abandoned that which they should have been upon, except for one man. So now we're talking about the people who had remnants of truth of what that gospel was, near the time of the prophet. Very few were actually having the true beliefs, and these were remnants of the scriptures, remnants of the Torah and the gospel.", "He said to him: except one person, a man in Mosul. So [Salman] went to him, and then he informed him about another person, and then in the end a bishop told him: I don't know anyone else that is on the same faith as us. At that time he's definitely not talking about Christians, because there was millions of Christians. So he was talking about a specific belief, from those who didn't alter, change their beliefs and scriptures. So he said to him: I don't know anyone else, but there's a prophet that is going to come. And then he gave him signs and descriptions of that prophet. They're given these descriptions from their books, which are supposed to be the gospel. He said he will immigrate from the lands of the Arabs, migrate between the two lava fields and palm trees. He will have signs that cannot be hidden. He takes gifts if someone gives him gifts, but he doesn't take charity. He doesn't eat from charity. And between his two shoulders there is a seal of the prophethood.", "These Christian beliefs are supposed to be in the gospel. We don't have them today. None of the texts that we have today contains this information. This is teachings from the true gospel, remnants of truth that still survive to that time. So from these examples we can clearly see that whatever we have today is not what we call original Torah, gospel. They are corrupted, because we do not have this information that the Quran tells us about. From an Islamic perspective, therefore, we believe that corruption have taken place.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Christian Dilemma: Do Muslims Believe The Bible Is Corrupted? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3bEZW_kx7Xg", ((4016, "1:06:56–1:07:39"), (4064, "1:07:44–1:08:15"), (4101, "1:08:21–1:08:57"), (4137, "1:08:57–1:09:58"), (4198, "1:09:58–1:11:03"), (4270, "1:11:10–1:11:53"), (4313, "1:11:53–1:12:53"), (4373, "1:12:53–1:13:29"),), id: 4657)
