#passage(("The [Injil] is a revelation that God has given to Jesus, peace be upon him. God was revealing to him guidance which he can give and deliver to his people. The same thing happened with Prophet Muhammad. We recorded, for instance, the hadith where God revealed revelation to prophet Muhammad, telling Prophet Muhammad to say to the people to do this or not to do that. So Jesus, when he was walking, also he had revelation being revealed to him, and he told it to his people: for example, to worship God alone, not to associate any partners with God, or they're going to be punished for associating partners. He told the people to follow the commandments of God, told people to be good to their neighbors. God revealed to him that guidance. The same thing happened with the other previous messengers. They had revelation that was sent to them by God.", "Now, that injil, which you refer to as the gospel, that was revealed to Jesus, that he was teaching his people: the scholars of Islam have two positions. Some scholars do have a position that the injil was written down. Some have the position that it wasn't written down. So you can take either position. I'm of the position it wasn't written down, meaning it wasn't written down at the life of Jesus, because Jesus was sent only to the children of Israel. It's explicit in the Quran. Allah says: and a messenger to the children of Israel. And it's also explicit in the Bible, in Matthew 15:24, where he says to the [Canaanite] woman: [I've] been only sent to the lost sheep of the house of Israel. Now, if Jesus is only for those people, there's no necessity for that scripture to be written down.", "Whatever Jesus told the people to do and not to do, and the guidance that he gave, later on some people have recorded some of these statements, but they recorded it from hearsay. They didn't record it with the elaborate historical system. That's why you have conflicting sources, conflicting manuscripts, conflicting sources that would say things that conflict with each other, and then you have to try and work out, and then you have liars and people doing [misattributions]. You have all of that in history, as it is normally with any type of history that doesn't have an elaborate system that you can determine what is true and what is false from. So you have all of these writings, and then you have Christianity having this major shift when the Roman Empire adopts Christianity, the Roman Empire, which has all of these Greek mythology and ideologies of God and sons of God coming to die for the world. The ideas of trinity and triune gods, these all existed in Greek mythology. It's not something new to Christianity.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Passionate Christian Argues For The Trinity With A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ntsF1iRj8IM", ((86, "1:26–2:19"), (139, "2:19–3:04"), (198, "3:18–4:16"),), id: 4659)
