#passage(("There's no tafseer of ibn 'Abbas. That's the first problem that you get from following anti-Islam Christian guys, who think they know what they're talking about, and they don't know what they're talking about. People commonly say there's something that's called tafseer ibn 'Abbas, which doesn't exist. Now, atTabari is an example of something more authoritative than ibn Kathir. It's way older than ibn Kathir. And atTabari reports directly from the students of the Companions, and their students. So what atTabari does is he gives different views and opinions of the righteous predecessors, and it's not translated into the English language, because it's so massive. Even ibn Kathir's is not fully translated. It's just that a brief version of ibn Kathir is translated. So now imagine atTabari, which is way bigger than ibn Kathir: it's not translated into the English language. It has voluminous amounts of explanations on each verse, and it brings the Narrations from the students of the Companions, and what they say.", "Now these Narrations will contain that the Jews and the Christians corrupted the Torah, they will contain that they corrupted the Scriptures with their own hand. And most importantly, I brought the Narration of ibn 'Abbas, which is in Bukhari, which explicitly says that the people of the Scriptures, including Jews and Christians, have corrupted their Scriptures. AtTabari, his opinion himself, is not what is authoritative for us. AtTabari goes through the verse, and different statements in the verse, and then he brings the statements of the students of the Companions, and the Companions, about the meaning of these verses, the people who directly learned from the Prophet. Our tafaseer does say that this is them corrupting the Torah. Ibn Kathir says the same thing! They don't say contradictory things.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Gets Busted By Muslim After Misquoting Islamic Sources! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bc55B6ult3c"