#passage(("There is a Hadith from 'Abdullah Ibn 'Abbas, where he talks about the Books of the People of the Scriptures, generally, how they're corrupted, both of them. And he's the cousin of the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, and he's the one who interpreted the Quran; the Prophet made a Du'a for him, a supplication that God gives him understanding of Quran and religion. And we have this narration of 'Abdullah Ibn 'Abbas. We have a narration from the Prophet himself as well.", "Another evidence I'm going to give you is the Quran itself correcting the previous scriptures clearly. It corrects the crucifixion. The Quran is telling the People of the Scriptures: Do not say falsehood about Allah (alImran3:71-75), and do not say that there are three in one (alMaida5:73), do not say that Jesus is God (anNisa4:171), do not worship Jesus and Mary (alMaida5:116), do not say Trinity (anNisa4:171). Jesus was not crucified on the cross (anNisa4:157). The prophets were moral people (alAnaam6:82-87). God did not rest on the Sabbath (Qaf50:38). And all of these things are mentioned in the Quran, addressing the People of the Scripture directly.", "We were not 1400 years believing in the corruption when we have no evidences for it. Our evidences for the corruption are many: the verses of the Quran that I mentioned to you, the Ahadith and narrations from 'Abdullah Ibn 'Abbas and the Prophet, the fact that the Quran refutes the false beliefs and doctrines that have been developed later on that are not from God, and the description of the Quran of certain things that should exist in the Torah and Injil that don't exist in the Torah and Injil today. For example the Quran (alFath48:29) mentions the description of the Companions of the Prophet being in the Torah and Injil; doesn't exist, we don't see it there. Many other things like this. So there's many reasons that scholars have used to show the people: here is a clear evidence that these Books have been corrupted.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Misinformed Christian Embarrasses Himself In Discussion With A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jhFvKCE57QI", ((357, "5:57–6:20"), (398, "6:38–7:18"), (450, "7:30–8:11"),), id: 4686)
