#passage(("When I was preparing some of these statements, it took me hours and hours because there's so many of them, and I didn't know which one to pick. And it's always laughable for me when someone makes this accusation or claim: oh, actually, Muslims believe that the Bible is not corrupt. It's crazy.", "Now what about from hadith? From the hadith, first we have the statements of [Ibn Abbas], where he tells us: why do you ask the people of the scripture about anything, while the book you have is revealed from Allah and has never been changed, and it is the newer and the latest revelation? You read it pure, unchanged, undistorted. And Allah told you the people of the book, i.e. Jews and Christians, changed their scripture, distorted them and wrote the scriptures with their own hand and claimed it is from Allah. [We've] been reading the verses from the Quran, and [that] is what [Ibn Abbas] is talking about; he's explaining the verses.", "Also [Abu Hurairah] narrates that the [Prophet] said: if the people of the book narrate to you something, they may be telling you something false and you believe it, and they may be telling you something that is true and you disbelieve in it. And if they did not corrupt their scripture, they would only be saying truth. Whenever they narrate their scripture, they would be telling us truth. But it is because they've corrupted their scripture, the prophet told us not to believe or disbelieve in what they say, meaning to be agnostic, unless that agrees explicitly with what we have; then we'll accept it.", "Now also we have a narration [Al-Hakim] narrates: the companion of the prophet Muhamad, he went to Sham, Levant, and he saw the Christians prostrate to their bishops and priests, and he also saw the Jews prostrate to the rabbis. So he asked those Jews and Christians: why do you do this? So they said: this is the greetings of the prophets. Then said: then it's better that we do this to our prophet. So when he went to the [Prophet], the prophet forbade him, and he told him that those Jews and Christians, they lied about their prophets just as they corrupted and distorted their book. This is a narration that is authentic, and he says according to the standards of [Bukhari] and Muslim.", "Also the prophet said that the children of Israel wrote a book, they followed [it] and left the Torah. This narration is authenticated also. The prophet told us that the children of Israel, as time has passed, their hearts became hardened, and they invented a book by themselves, and that book took over their hearts and their tongues.", "This was at the time of [Uthman], the third caliphate of Islam, and there was some Muslims, because Islam spread so far and wide, that disagreed when they were reciting the Quran. They were new Muslims. They had issues in their recitations and they made mistakes. And then when [Hudhayfah] came to [Uthman], he said: set these people right, set them straight before they disagree about the book the way the Jews and the Christians disagreed about the book. So now it's explicitly telling you, this is in [Bukhari], that this is what the companions believe, what the [khalifah] believe. This is what Muslims believed at the time. The evidences are many and overwhelming, and I believe I've mentioned more than sufficient evidences from the Quran and hadith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Christian Dilemma: Do Muslims Believe The Bible Is Corrupted? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3bEZW_kx7Xg", ((3794, "1:03:14–1:03:36"), (3816, "1:03:36–1:04:01"), (3846, "1:04:06–1:04:41"), (3881, "1:04:41–1:05:15"), (3915, "1:05:15–1:06:02"), (3976, "1:06:16–1:06:56"),), id: 4687)
