#refbox("Reference text: sunnah.com, Sahih al-Bukhari 2685", (("", "Narrated Ubaidullah bin `Abdullah bin `Utba:"), ("", "Ibn `Abbas said, \"O Muslims? How do you ask the people of the Scriptures, though your Book (i.e. the Qur'an) which was revealed to His Prophet is the most recent information from Allah and you recite it, the Book that has not been distorted? Allah has revealed to you that the people of the scriptures have changed with their own hands what was revealed to them and they have said (as regards their changed Scriptures): This is from Allah, in order to get some worldly benefit thereby.\" Ibn `Abbas added: \"Isn't the knowledge revealed to you sufficient to prevent you from asking them? By Allah I have never seen any one of them asking (Muslims) about what has been revealed to you.\""),))
// U ML102:264-512 | The Muslim Lantern | 6
#passage(("When you read a bad translation, you think ibn 'Abbas is saying that they're writing a separate Book, when ibn 'Abbas is referring to both the Torah and the Gospel. And anyone who can read Arabic knows that! What does ibn 'Abbas say? يَا مَعْشَرَ المُسْلِمِينْ (O Muslims) كيفَ تَسْأَلُونَ أهْلَ الكِتَابِ عَنْ شَيْء (how do you ask the people of the Scriptures) وكِتَابُكُمُ الذي أُنْزِلَ علَى نَبِيِّهِ (and your Book that Allah sent down upon His Messenger,) (ie, the Quran – the most recent news you're reading it, and there is no corruption in it). Nobody has changed it, nothing happened to it. (And Allah has told you that the people of the Book has CHANGED the Book of Allah.) Changed which Book? وغَيَّرُوا بأَيْدِيهِمُ الكِتَابَ (They wrote with their hand الكِتَابَ alKitab (the Book)).", "\"alKitab\" here in the Arabic language has two letters الـ (Alif and Lam) for identification, meaning it's for معرفة (ma'rifa). It's referring to something which we already mentioned, ie, the Torah and the Gospel, the Books of the people of the Scriptures. So 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas is saying explicitly that the people of the Scriptures have changed the Book of Allah. Which Book of Allah? Was that a different Book? No! He's referring to the Torah and the Gospel. There's no other Book of Allah that they were changing. They wrote the Book with their own hands, (and then they said it is from Allah, so they can buy with it a mere price). (Isn't that enough for you? Didn't it come to you enough?), meaning from the Quran, that you go and ask them? You don't need to go and ask them! And we don't see them coming and asking you.", "Where does it say in the statement of ibn 'Abbas \"another Book\"? All it says is \"the Book\". That is a clear misrepresentation of the Arabic text.", "So this is your argument: the Torah and the Gospel are here, and I go write another Book, and me writing another book is changing the Torah and the Gospel! Whose reasoning is that? When we read the clear translation, we know that makes no sense. You cannot change one thing by writing another. When you write another, you write another thing; you don't change the same thing. You can only change the same thing by changing its own content.", "Everyone, go open ibn Kathir yourself, copy paste the Arabic, and put it into Google translation or chat GPT or anything. Not a single one of them is going to translate \"another Book\" for you.", "We only use Quran.com to view Quran translations. It's not authoritative in any way, shape, or form, in the tafasir of the Quran, in the Hadith, in any of these things.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Gets Busted By Muslim After Misquoting Islamic Sources! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bc55B6ult3c", ((860, "14:20–15:05"), (908, "15:08–16:23"), (1017, "16:57–17:49"), (1194, "19:54–20:25"), (1251, "20:51–20:59"), (1317, "21:57–22:03"),), id: 4689)
