#passage(("Ibn Kathir said other things. Here he just quotes 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, but he quotes other people as well in the tafseer. So ibn Kathir here, he reports from ibn Jarir, from Ibrahim, from Hammad, from 'Abdul Hamid, from Kinanah, etc., from 'Uthman Ibn 'Affan, which is the Caliphate of Islam and the Companion of the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, that the Prophetﷺ recited the verse, and then the Prophet said.. He is reporting this Narration. Now, regardless of how weak or strong this Narration is, because ibn Kathir says it is غريب (ghareeb: solitary), he reports this Narration. What does this Narration say? \"It says that the Prophetﷺ said: Woe الويل (alWayl) is a mountain in Jahannam (Hellfire).\" \"And this verse was revealed to the Jews لأنهم حرّفوا التوراة (They distorted the Torah).\" \"They added in it what they like, and they removed from it what they hated.\" \"And they deleted the name of the Prophet Muhammadﷺ in the Torah.\" \"And that's why Allah has anger with them.\" And this is a statement in ibn Kathir.", "So what happens here is, when we go to ibn Kathir and read everything ibn Kathir says, we see that ibn Kathir keeps refuting your dilemma, one after one, after one. Somehow you Christians think you're going to go to our own tafaseer, and you're going to refute our own tradition from our own tafaseer. It just ends up backfiring in your face when we actually read what they said.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Gets Busted By Muslim After Misquoting Islamic Sources! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bc55B6ult3c", ((1696, "28:16–29:27"), (1775, "29:35–30:04"),), id: 4691)
