#passage(("There's two ways to understand this. First, that this Narration is not authentic, which is said by many different scholars. We can just simply say that we don't accept the authenticity of this Narration, and therefore all your story does not work anymore. I want to say something very important: whenever I say that we don't accept the authenticity of this Narration, I can bring you books of people who died over a thousand years ago who were saying this Narration is not authentic. So it's not me today, because I didn't like it, or a group of Muslims didn't like it today, so we say it's not authentic. But we have a long history of people telling us what is authentic and what is not authentic, and the Christians just newly figured out this information.", "Another easy way to answer it: if you want to accept this Narration, how do you explain it? We say simply that the Quran addresses the people and uses the term the Torah and the Injeel for what the Christians and the Jews hold in their hand, even though the same Quran affirms that they're being corrupted. Why does the Quran use the term Torah and the Injeel? Because they call it the Torah and the Injeel. So if they call it the Torah and the Injeel, how can the Quran refer to it then? What other word the Quran is going to use? Quran will use the same term that they use in order for them to understand it's addressing what they have in their hand.", "So when the Prophetﷺ uses the term Torah there, he does not mean that this is the exact Torah that was given in the hand. He means that they call it Torah. So when he says \"I believe in you\", meaning we believe in the Torah that was revealed to Moses directly by the Creator, we have no issues with that, and the One Who revealed to you, which is Allah. We believe that Allah revealed the Torah to Musa عليه السلام (Peace be upon him); we don't have any issues with that. The issue is only when you take one verse and you remove it from the entire context. You cannot take that Hadith and remove it from the context of the Quran that says it's corrupted, from the context of other Hadiths that say it's corrupted, that says that these people do not have the exact same Manuscripts in their hand today. You cannot pick one thing and then pretend that this is the case and ignore everything else.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Claims The Quran Contains Satanic Verses?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=27xa01f05ag", ((823, "13:43–14:11"), (856, "14:16–14:38"), (883, "14:43–15:15"),), id: 4694)
