#passage(("Chapter:2, Verse:41: do not exchange what? \"My verses\", بِـَٔايَـٰتِى. But what does that mean then? What is the exchange that they're doing for a small price here? The verse in Arabic says \"Ayati\". \"Ayati\" here could mean a number of different things. You could take an interpretation that this refers to exchanging worldly desires and ignoring the signs of God, or you could take even that this is referring to changing the Word of God, because in other parts of the Quran it mentions that they CHANGE the words of God for a mere price (alBaqara2:79), so they can get things in the worldly desires; they corrupted and changed the Scripture.", "But generally, this verse, who is it talking to? It's talking to the Children of Israel. So now, in this verse, Allah is saying to the children of Israel to (believe in) what? (That which was sent down): the Quran, مُصَدِّقًۭا (confirming that which is with you). What does that mean? Let me tell you what atTabari actually says, not what a random website tells you \"atTabari says\".", "So here atTabari says: وَءَامِنُوا۟ بِمَآ أَنزَلْتُ مُصَدِّقًۭا لِّمَا مَعَكُمْ (and believe in that which was revealed confirming that which you have) :يقول (He says) -referring to Allah- Allah says: يا مَعْشَرَ أهْلِ الكِتابِ (Ô group of People of the Book) ءَامِنُوا۟ بِمَآ أَنزَلْتُ مُصَدِّقًۭا لِّمَا مَعَكُمْ (believe in the Quran, which is confirming that which you have with you) يقول: (Allah says:) لأنهم يجدون محمدًاﷺ (Because they find Prophet Muhammadﷺ, salla Allah 'alayhi wa sallam: peace and blessings of God be upon Him) (written down in the Torah and the Injeel). That is what the verse is referring to. This is what atTabari says.", "Allah is saying: (believe in the Quran confirming that which you have with you). So the Quran is confirming the same thing which is present in your book, which is the Prophethood of Prophet Muhammad! So \"believe\", i.e. referring to the Prophet: believe in the Prophet and the Quran, and do not be the first person to disbelieve in the Prophet and the Quran, because the Quran is only confirming that which you have with you, which is the Prophethood of Muhammad. Very simple explanation, which is what atTabari is saying.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “King James Christian Challenges Muslim On Bible Preservation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eSGX_1-ukxw", ((582, "9:42–11:43"), (707, "11:47–12:55"), (779, "12:59–13:36"), (845, "14:05–14:35"),), id: 4708)
