#passage(("Affirming the previous scriptures, what does it mean? It means the Quran affirms that there was a scripture that revealed in the past called the Tawra. That's what the Quran affirms, number one. Number two, the Quran affirms that within that scripture the description of Prophet Muhammad. That's what affirming here means. It affirms that Allah sent prophets in the past, and he sent scriptures with these prophets, and that those prophets foretold prophet Muhammad. That is the only understanding we take from that.", "Now, confirms never was used in language to necessarily mean that something is preserved. Preserved is a word and confirm is a word. I can confirm this idea that there was previous prophets and messengers, this idea that prophet Muhammad has mentioned these scriptures; that does not mean that I'm saying that these scriptures are preserved, because the Quran, all over the other verses, talks about the corruption of these scriptures. Open any book from the time of the prophet until today; all of them will tell you confirm means what I told you it means.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How Do You Know Which Religion Is From God? A Detailed Comprehensive Analysis | The Muslim Lantern”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9F5gS1yWIRI", ((4228, "1:10:28–1:11:01"), (4266, "1:11:06–1:11:42"),), id: 4709)
