#passage(("The word 'Bible' does not exist in the Quran from beginning to end. So to claim that the Quran affirms the Bible is a lie, with all due respect, because the word Bible does not exist.", "Before I respond to that, I'll say to you clearly, it's irrelevant to what the Bible says in relation with Quran, because right now I'm talking to you about the scripture that you believe. So what I believe has got nothing to do with what you believe. So you're supposed to respond based on your belief, because that's your scripture. But what Christians end up doing is to bring our belief into their belief, because they know they're stuck. They've got nothing that they can respond to. So now they have to go into the Quran for some reason, like last straw or something. We don't accept that this scripture has been preserved anyways, so it's not something that we have to look at and investigate and believe in what it says.", "The Quran doesn't say 'the Bible', the word 'Bible'. The second thing is, Quran says Torah and Injeel. Does the Quran say the Tawrat was given to Moses, and the Injil was given to Jesus? I'll tell you, it does. Allahﷻ says in the Quran (alMaida5:46) وَءَاتَیۡنَـٰهُ ٱلۡإِنجِیلَ (and We gave him the Injeel). So if the Injeel was given to Jesus, is what you have today something which was given to Jesus, or written later on? What you have in your hand, what you call the Bible, is not what was given to Jesus and Moses, but people later on wrote history of what they thought Jesus said, or Moses. The Bible itself records, it says that Jesus went to Galilee and he preached the Gospel (Mark1:14-15). So there was a Gospel that Jesus was preaching, that Gospel that Jesus was preaching when he was alive, not that which was written later on after him. It's that which we believe in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Disproves Christianity Using A Single Question! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nIlC0UJ1DPg", ((1251, "20:51–21:05"), (1302, "21:42–22:16"