#passage(("I said there's truth in it. I was telling you in the beginning there's truth and falsehood, because people are not going to change everything. So I give you an example of what truth is: that there's only one God. \"There's no God besides me.\" So I don't have a problem with that.", "I'm not picking and choosing anything, because I don't follow the Old Testament or the Bible. You do. The one who picks and chooses: the one who follows. You are asking me as a Muslim what I agree with and what I disagree with in your book. That doesn't mean I pick and choose. That means, if I am a Muslim, I have my own faith and belief. If something agrees with my own faith and belief, I don't have an issue with it.", "The statement of truth and falsehood refers to that which agrees or disagrees with revelation. Shakespeare has true information. The Harry Potter story has true information. Like, if Shakespeare says all human beings die, the Quran says human beings die; therefore, Shakespeare has truth. There's a true statement written in a book. What's the problem with that?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Niqabi Challenges the Continuity of Islam with Previous Scriptures! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7-kSmD09rxI", ((1576, "26:16–26:29"), (1595, "26:35–27:04"), (1636, "27:16–27:46"),), id: 4718)
