#passage(("I'm going to mention a few examples, which are another type of evidence that the Quran corrects the beliefs of Christians and addresses Christians directly. For example, about the trinity. Allah says: people of the book, do not exaggerate in your religion, and do not say about Allah except the truth; do not say three. Allah says those who say Allah is three, they have committed disbelief. So Allah is explicitly talking to the Christians. He knows the Christians believe in these things. So that would mean that the Christians now have corrupted beliefs, corrupted traditions. Those corrupted beliefs and corrupted traditions Allah is correcting in the Quran, because they do not have the original teachings of the Torah, the gospel.", "Same thing for Jesus being God. Allah says in the Quran that those who say Jesus is Allah or God have committed disbelief. So Allah is clearly refuting this idea. Also, the Quran is teaching that Jesus never taught divinity, let alone just claim to be God. He never taught divinity, and the Quran says Allah will question Jesus on day of judgment: did you say to the people to take you as a god? And he will say no. And also the Quran says that Jesus sent only to those sheep of the house of Israel, refuting any idea of any Christians who believe, or some verses that are corrupted, that claims that he was sent to everyone. Allah says: and a messenger to the children of Israel, specifically.", "The idea of God resting and refreshing on the seventh day, that exists in the Old Testament, that Christians and Jews believe: Allah says in the Quran, created the heavens and earth in six days, and no tiredness or fatigue have ever touched us. Allah explicitly refutes these beliefs. Those people believe these things. So you know clearly that the author of the Quran, he knows the beliefs of these people, and is refuting those beliefs to show us that what they believe is not the original beliefs.", "Also the prophets of God, for example, they are