ieve in.", "Now secondly, when you jump into verse 47, what you're doing there is you're jumping ahead. You're ignoring the other verses. When you go to the next verse after the verse that you read, it says: We reveal the Torah, within it guidance and light. And then it says the prophets can judge by what Allah has revealed. Then it says: with what they were entrusted to protect, these scriptures. So Allah, when he revealed the scriptures (this is talking about now in the past), Allah revealed the Tawra and then he entrusted the rabbis and the people of knowledge to protect it, to preserve it, and they were told to judge. The end of the verses say \"and judge\". Then the next verse mentions some of the teachings in the Torah.", "This is a chronological order. You can read it yourself. It starts by: Allah revealed the Tawra. Then told the people of the Tawra to follow the Tawra, protect the Tawra. Then after that Allah sends (see, chronological order) Allah sends Jesus in their footsteps with the [Injil]. Then Allah tells the people of the [Injil] to judge with the [Injil].", "Then what you miss is the next verse, which refutes you. Then the chronological order now comes to the Quran: then we reveal to you the Quran. Then what does Allah say in that verse? He says to judge between them with the Quran. Between who? People of the book. Everybody. He's not telling you to follow your book. He's telling you to follow the Quran. Allah says, \"And do not follow their desires and do not be afraid from them. Judge between them in the Quran, with what Allah has revealed to you.\" Then the verse after it repeats the same thing again: \"And judge between them with the Quran, with what we have revealed to you, and do not follow.\" Why is Allah repeating it twice? Because there are some Christians who think the Quran is saying follow the scriptures. No, it's not. It's just giving you a chronological order of what happened.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Educated Christian Challenges Muslim On Bible Corruption And Textual Criticism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gYYmqGjrSmo", ((1215, "20:15–20:55"), (1283, "21:23–22:04"), (1326, "22:06–23:11"), (1398, "23:18–24:13"), (1460, "24:20–24:40"), (1480, "24:40–25:25"),), id: 4729)
