#passage(("Now a lot of the Christians, unfortunately, think that this verse, when it says (Ask those who were reading the Book before you), refers to those who are reciting the Book. No! Those who were reciting the Book, many of them accepted Islam. And anyone can go, for example, any Tafsir (Exegesis): atTabari, alQurtubi, any of these Tafasir (Tafsirs), and you will see that they say those who were reciting the Book before you are like 'Abdullah ibn Salam, who's someone who was from the People of the Book and accepted Islam. You had people like Ka'b alAhbar, Salman alFarisi. All of them were People of the Book who were reading whatever they had, remnants from the Torah and Injeel, or whatever they had in their capacity; they read it, and they accepted Prophet Muhammad and they believed in him as a Messenger. So this verse in the Quran is saying: go to those Believers, people who became believers, People of the Book.", "And the Quran uses the term the \"People of the Book\" about the believers. Allah says: (and from the People of the Book who believed) (alimran3:199). So Allah calls the People of the Book, but still calls them believers. So, in Chapter:3 of the Quran, verse:199, (And from the People of the Book وَإِنَّ مِنْ أَهْلِ ٱلْكِتَـٰبِ who believe in Allah) (And what was revealed to YOU). What was revealed to us? The Quran! So these people are already Muslims. There's no doubt that these people are Muslims, because they believe in Allah, and they believe in that which was revealed to us. So Allah calls them أهل الكتاب and says that they believe in that which was revealed to US (And they believe in Allah, and they believe in the verses of Allah, and they don't sell it for a mere price) (They will have the reward with their Lord). So when Allah tells us in the Quran to ask those who were reading the Book, the Quran is referring to the believers from those who were reading the Book, according to the exegesis of the Muslims and the other verses of the Quran, which identifies the People of the Book being people who are actually BELIEVERS.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Angry Christian Rage Quits After Confronting Muslim On Jesus In The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XtxFdX7yIAs", ((1250, "20:50–21:28"), (1297, "21:37–22:35"),), id: 4747)
