#passage(("Allahﷻ says in the Quran: أَفَغَيْرَ ٱللَّهِ أَبْتَغِى حَكَمًۭا (Do I seek any judge other than Allah?), in the verse before (6:114). So here حَكَمًۭا means someone who sets a ruling or a judgment, or sets something. And then Allah says: (Those who are given the Scripture, they know that it was sent down to you from your Lord with the Truth) (so do not be from those who doubt). Then Allah says (and the Word of your Lord has been..) تَــــمَّــــتْ. What does it mean? \"Completed\" or \"perfected\". What does that refer to? That is not referring to the Quran, because the Quran was not perfected or completed when this verse was revealed. That is referring to \"the promise of Allah\", to \"the judgement of Allah\". So the verse before it mentions حَكَمًۭا (judge); the next verse is confirming that the judgment of Allah has been fulfilled (the judgment of your Lord). So it's not referring to the Quran, it's referring to the judgment of Allah.", "Now, the word 'word', even in English, has many meanings: it can mean a ruling, a promise, or it can mean an actual word. So when I say to you \"I gave you my word\", it doesn't mean \"my word\" I just put it in a box and give it to you! It just means \"I promised\", \"I made a promise\". So, here when it says \"the words\" (there is no changing in \"the words\"), meaning in the judgment, in the promises that Allahﷻ makes. That is what it means.", "And you can go back to the Tafasir. Here, atTabari says: حدّثنا بِشر (Bishr reported to us, that Yazid reported to us) (that Saeed reported to us, that Qatada reported to us), and then he mentions the relevant part of the verse. This is atTabari's methodology. وَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ (and the Word of your Lord have been fulfilled..) (..there is no changing in His Words). Then atTabari says: \"Allah is saying:\" صدقًا وعدلًا فيما حَكَم (Truthful and Just in that which He has judged). So, He's talking about judgment. The verse is talking about judgment. It's not talking about the Quran or the verses of Allah, as some Christians try to \"word-salad\" the verses and try to present it to us. That's a very common argument they come up with, but sadly it's a basic 101 Tafsir.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “King James Christian Challenges Muslim On Bible Preservation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eSGX_1-ukxw", ((1355, "22:35–23:36"), (1419, "23:39–24:05"), (1447, "24:07–25:01"),), id: 4748)
