#passage(("Now, according to the brilliant minds of the Christian apologists, Muhammad, peace be upon Him, invented this new religion. He went to the Christians and he told them: I believe Jesus is a prophet, he's not a deity, and you people are going to go to hell. However, at the same time, according to them, he's affirming their books as divine revelation, despite having no idea what's in those books.", "Allegedly, you had Jews and Christians, including a rabbi, a major Rabbi, Abdullah Bin Salam, converting to Islam after coming across this, for some reason. Despite their books conflicting with the Quran and conflicting with the teachings of Muhammad, [peace be] upon him, they still didn't see that to be a problem. Strange. Now there's another aspect of this theory which makes things a lot worse, which a lot of people don't appreciate, which is that a lot of these critics of Islam believe that Muhammad, peace be upon him, actually plagiarize the Bible: the Quran and the Hadith stole ideas, passages and teachings directly from the Bible.",), "Farid Responds, “The Dumbest Argument against Islam EVER!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WhcJLgflN-E", ((131, "2:11–2:38"), (240, "4:00–4:39"),), id: 4753)
