#passage(("The claim is this: the Quran affirms the Bible, this whole Islamic dilemma stuff. The Quran affirms the Bible, and if the Quran affirms the Bible and the Bible includes information that contradicts the Quran, despite the Bible allegedly being preserved, therefore Islam is false. And if that's the case, then the person, the Muslim that's hearing this and accepting this, needs to leave Islam. True, but that doesn't prove that the Bible is preserved, because once you leave Islam, you no longer trust in Muhammad, peace be upon him. So you would still need some sort of secular approach, or at least some sort of historical approach, to prove that the Bible is preserved.", "In the debate, which was about the authenticity of scriptures, Sam and Jay didn't really bring much of a positive argument for the reliability of the Bible. All that was brought forward was this argument to Muslims, which was: Islamic dilemma, Muhammad, peace be upon him, affirms the preservation and authority of the previous scriptures. But that's not convincing to a Christian, it's not convincing to a Hindu, it's not convincing to an atheist, it's not even convincing to the Muslim, because again, when the Muslim accepts that point, the muslim's not going to believe in the Bible; [Muslim's] just going to disbelieve in Islam. So, to summarize, nothing they said can be used to prove that the Bible is authentic and preserved.", "It would actually take 40 minutes to go through all the verse numbers that [Shamoun] brought up in his debate, because [Shamoun] didn't even quote any of the verses. He didn't read them out; he just blurted out the numbers: 40 to 44, chapter 2 [verse] 89, chapter 2 verse 91, chapter 2 verse 101, chapter 2 verse 113, chapter 2 verse 121, chapter 2 verse 136. And of course David sees nothing wrong with this. Naturally, he considers [Ijaz] and Daniel to be at fault for not being able to respond to all of this, because they should have had the verses memorized in Arabic, they should have had the numbers memorized, they should have recognized that some of the wordings in some of the verses are repetitive, and because they failed to do that in five minutes, it's their fault; definitely not a sly tactic by [Shamoun] in order to overwhelm [Ijaz] and Daniel.",), "Farid Responds, “Don't tell Sam Shamoun about this Video!!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C4P3sNDhViU", ((208, "3:28–4:13"), (275, "4:35–5:24"), (333, "5:33–6:29"),), id: 4755)
