#passage(("If you're now comparing Christianity and Islam, you look at the Bible. If you look at the Bible, you'll see the book of Ezekiel, that we have these verses that talk about puberty. And we have people using it. But even that doesn't talk about the right age of marriage or whatever, but it talks about women being ready, and then it refers to puberty. For example, development of certain body parts. Because it's detailed and it's not really appropriate for all ages, I'm not going to say what the verses are saying, but you get the point I'm making. It talks about certain body parts.. let's just say puberty, the development that is related to puberty.", "Now, puberty can range all the way from 8 years old to 13 years old - we're talking today. What is the source for that? For example, the NHS - the National Health Service in the UK - will tell you that puberty can range all the way from 8 years old all the way to 13 years old. So under the biblical narrative, this range from 8 to 13 is completely valid. Why is it completely valid? Because it is the age of puberty. And if you're basing it on Ezekiel, then that would be the case.", "If we look at the Bible, it talks about, for example, the book of Numbers, chapter:31, verse:17 and 18. There's a command there, where Moses commands his army, Moses the Prophet of God. He commands his army during war to capture the little girls that have not yet known a man for themselves. And the word there in Hebrew, it's about \"children\" - so \"little girls-children\", \"child-girls\" - to take them for themselves, \"that have not yet known a man\": who have not had intercourse with a man, they didn't do anything with a man. And the Bible has an explicit command to go and take these girls for themselves.", "Now we get Christians saying, \"Of course, they're going to do this to them. They're going to do that..\" What are they going to do? They're going to take the little girls to do what with them exactly, in war?! They're going to take them to the kindergarten, which didn't exist at the time? Of course not! There's only one purpose you take women for it. And the emphasis on the idea of not knowing a man is there's only one reason why you'd take them. And you can read the biblical commentaries on these passages that will clearly talk about that.", "You can look at, for example, the marriage of Rebekah and Isaac in the Old Testament (Gen23:1). If you make a calculation of how old was Sarah and how old was Abraham, all of these calculations come to the conclusion that she was between 3 and 10 years old. You can't go more than 10; it was between 3 and 10 when she married Isaac. And we have Rabbis, in the Hebrew tradition, who'd explicitly tell you that it's OK to get married at the age of 3 - the age of 3 is the limit for them. They base it on this incident of Isaac and Rebekah. That's the objective fact. This is the biblical narrative.", "You look even the saints of Christianity, like Saint Athanasius, and all of these saints, you'll see many of them have had brides at the age of 12 years old, for example. The age of marriage in their time in the Roman Empire was 12 years old. And that's why the Catholic Encyclopaedia would record that Mary was 12 years old when she married Joseph.", "So this is Christianity. Nobody can come from a Christian or Jewish worldview and tell us a certain age is right and a certain age is wrong, because they don't have a sanction from God, a moral sanction, and an objective sanction, or something determined using God's command that will tell us this age is right and this age is wrong.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Confronts Muslim On The Marriage Of The Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vz1jgBpf8UE", ((470, "7:50–8:18"), (504, "8:24–8:55"), (539, "8:59–9:40"), (586, "9:46–10:09"), (613, "10:13–10:56"), (662, "11:02–11:18"), (688, "11:28–11:40"),), id: 4840)
