#passage(("There's no specific age over here, and the verse seems completely open to interpretation, but that's just one of the many issues with this verse. So before even going deep into this, I'd like to point out that this specific passage isn't even a command from the Holy Spirit, as per Paul's admission. Paul says about [virgins]: \"I have no command from the Lord, but I do give an opinion as one who by the Lord's Mercy is trustworthy.\" So Paul is just giving his opinion; he isn't claiming that there is some sort of inspiration going on here.", "But what I find really interesting about the quote that Avery is providing is that there's a little footnote above \"past marriageable age\", and that footnote says \"if his passions are strong\". Now the reason why it's saying this is because there seems to be some sort of confusion surrounding the term [hyperakmos], and there's a difference of opinion as to whether this is referring to the male or the female in the verse, which is why you have famous Bibles translating this in a way that's completely different from the way Avery is presenting.", "The NIV says: \"If anyone is worried that he might not be acting honorably toward the Virgin he is engaged to, and if his passion are too strong and he feels he ought to marry, he should do as he wants.\" The ESV says: \"If anyone thinks that he is not behaving properly towards his [betrothed], if his passions are strong, and it has to be, let him do as he wishes: let them marry, it is no sin.\" The RSV says: \"If anyone thinks that he is not behaving properly towards his [betrothed], if his passions are strong, and it has to be, let him do as he wishes: let them marry, it is no sin.\" Out of these three, only the NIV mentions age of the Virgin, as an alternative translation, and instead it says \"if she is getting beyond the usual age for marriage\". So from the get-go we got multiple issues.",), "Farid Responds, “Godlogic and Age of Marriage in Bible”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IW5TGYt5fEY", ((123, "2:03–2:43"), (163, "2:43–3:18"), (198, "3:18–4:13"),), id: 4844)
