doesn't rest, by definition. You don't rest and refresh unless you're weak.", "Also, the Bible says, when God saw the people doing bad, whatever - I believe it's also in Genesis (6:6-7) - it says God regrets creating man. Is regretting a deficiency or not? Regretting man is Genesis6:6: \"The Lord regretted that he made human beings on earth, and his heart was deeply troubled.\" This is Genesis, chapter:6, verse:6.", "About God being reminded, it's in Genesis, chapter:9, verse:13-16. Here it says: \"I have set my rainbow in the clouds, and it will be a sign for the covenant between me and the people. When I bring clouds over the earth, and a rainbow appears in the clouds, I will [REMEMBER] my covenant between me and all the living creatures of every kind. Never again will the waters become a flood to destroy all life.\"", "Genesis:32, verse:22-28: \"On that night, Jacob got up and took his two wives, his two female servants..\" \"Then when he saw a man that he could not overpower him, he touched Jacob's hip..\" \"The man said, 'Let me go, for its daybreak.' But Jacob said, 'I will not let you go unless you bless me'! The man asked him, 'What is your name?' Jacob answered, 'Jacob'. Then the man said, 'Your name will be no longer Jacob, but Israel, because you have struggled and wrestled with God and you have overcome'!\" So here it talks about God taking a human form, coming and wrestling with Jacob, and then Jacob overpowering God, where he said, \"Oh, look, God, I'm not going to let you go until you bless me, God!\" Then God is like, \"OK, let me go, I'm going to bless you now!\" Just think about this stuff! Think about this stuff and be like, \"OK, does that make any sense?\" No, it does not!", "You have, for example, Genesis2:2-3: \"By the seventh day, God had finished the work that he's been doing on the heavens. So He RESTED from all his work.\" Why did he rest? And then it says, \"He rested from ALL THE WORK OF CREATING that he had done.\" What is the reason he's resting? All the work that he's done, he's resting from it now. How is he not resting because He's tired? The other one, I believe, is in Exodus 31:17: \"It'll be a sign between me and the Israelites forever, for in six days the Lord has made the heavens and the earth, and on the seventh day, He rested and refreshed\" - or \"was refreshed\".",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Devout Christian Shocked After A Muslim Reveals The Truth About The Bible! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n0Yn0rYmS9s", ((449, "7:29–8:24"), (525, "8:45–9:25"), (584, "9:44–11:16"), (690, "11:30–11:58"), (738, "12:18–12:40"), (773, "12:53–13:58"), (844, "14:04–14:53"),), id: 4865)
